{
    "duration": 226.3800048828125,
    "language": "english",
    "text": "Hi, the Rainbow Puddle Adventure. Henry the Hedgehog loved rainy days, but he loved what came after even more. One spring morning, after a night of gentle showers, Henry peeked out from his cozy leaf pile home and saw puddles dotting the forest floor. Today feels like a special day for exploring, Henry whispered to himself as he slipped on his tiny blue boots. Henry had just started his morning walk when he noticed something extraordinary. In the largest puddle, right beside the old oak tree, colors were dancing on the water's surface. Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet swirled together like a rainbow had fallen from the sky. A rainbow puddle, Henry gasped, his paws clapping with excitement. I've never seen anything so beautiful. As Henry leaned closer, his reflection rippled through the colors. He wondered if the puddle might be magical. Carefully, he dipped one paw into the edge of the puddle. The water felt warm and tingly. I should share this with someone, Henry thought. But Henry was new to this part of the forest and hadn't made any friends yet. Taking a deep breath, he decided to be brave. He followed a narrow path that wound between tall grasses and blooming wildflowers. Soon, he heard humming coming from behind a cluster of daisies. Hello, Henry called softly. A small rabbit with floppy ears peeked out. Oh, hello there. I'm Rosie, she said with a friendly smile. I'm Henry. I just found something amazing and I thought maybe you'd like to see it too? Rosie's eyes sparkled with curiosity. I love amazing things. Lead the way! Together they hurried back to the rainbow puddle, which seemed to shine even brighter now. Oh my, Rosie exclaimed. It's like the sky's most beautiful rainbow decided to take a swim. Watch this, Henry said, gently touching the puddle. Ripples of color spread outward like magical rings. Rosie tried too, giggling as the colors danced around her paw. We should invite others. Soon, Henry and Rosie had gathered a squirrel named Sam, two field mice sisters, and a shy turtle called Theo. Each animal took turns creating colorful ripples in the puddle. The colors are like us, Rosie observed thoughtfully. Different, but beautiful together. And more special when shared with friends, added Henry. As the afternoon sun began to drift lower, the rainbow puddle slowly started to fade. The animals watched as the colors grew softer until they disappeared completely. Will it come back tomorrow? Asked one of the mice. Maybe, Henry replied. But even if it doesn't, we found something even better than a rainbow puddle today. What's that? Asked Theo the turtle. Henry smiled at his new friends. We found each other. That night, as Henry snuggled into his leaf pile, he thought about his wonderful day. He had discovered that the most colorful adventures weren't just about finding magical rainbow puddles. They were about sharing those special moments with friends. And tomorrow promised new puddles and new adventures, all waiting to be explored together.",
